## 3. Verification

### 3.1 What is proven, mapped to each root cause

| Check | Root cause covered | Assertion |
|---|---|---|
| `outputMatchesReference` | RC1, RC2, RC3 | replay output is bit-for-bit (1e-12) equal to a strict submission-order renderer |
| `recoveryMatchesReference` / `recoveryTriggered` | RC4 | output after a simulated device loss is identical and exactly one retry occurred |
| `peakEqualsTightBound` / `peakWithinCapacity` | RC1, §2.3 | measured peak equals `max_t ceil(n_t/ceil(n_t/C))` and never exceeds `C` |
| `passesMinimal` | RC1 | replay bin count equals `sum_t ceil(n_t/C)` |
| `allFragmentsOnce` | RC1 | the partition is exact: every fragment is in exactly one bin |
| `[2]` shuffle invariance | RC3 | permuting the input array while keeping `seq` does not change output |
| `[2b]` blend law | RC2 | `(a∘b)∘c = a∘(b∘c)`, `a∘b ≠ b∘a`, and regrouping across a bin boundary is exact |
| `[4]` exhaustive enumeration | §2.3 | for all `n<=18, C<=6`, no minimum-bin partition beats the balanced max |
| `[5]` 200 random graphs | all | combined properties hold on randomized tiles/passes/capacities |

